The project has a promising architecture, but several compile failures, security bugs, no-op control paths, accounting errors, and shutdown problems make it unsafe for production in its current form.

Highest-priority findings

| Priority | Area | Problem | Impact |
|---|---|---|---|
| P0 | Alerting | AlertingConfig and RamShieldError do not exist | Module cannot compile if included |
| P0 | IPC | Invalid IPs become 0.0.0.0 | Different invalid inputs alias one store key |
| P0 | IPC | BlockIp, UnblockIp, and Flush only return success text | Administrative commands do nothing |
| P0 | Detection | Reconstructed events lose status, fingerprint, and first timestamp | Threat scoring and rate calculations are corrupted |
| P0 | Shutdown | Detection and forecasting use independent/no shutdown state | Engine shutdown does not stop workers |
| P0 | Dashboard | Config mutation is unauthenticated, permissive-CORS, and unvalidated | Remote configuration takeover if exposed |
| P1 | Store | Replacement RAM accounting only adds growth and never subtracts shrinkage | RAM counter becomes inaccurate |
| P1 | Store | Expired get() entries are not removed or accounted | Memory remains occupied indefinitely |
| P1 | Detection | Subnet reverse index exists but subnet blocking still scans entire store | O(store size) hot path |
| P1 | IPC | Single-event path uses blocking send() inside async request handling | Tokio worker can block indefinitely |
| P1 | Metrics | Detection blocks are counted twice conceptually; total block counter is unused | Dashboard/Prometheus disagree |
| P1 | Config | Runtime patch replaces whole sections and skips validation | Invalid live configurations |
| P1 | Security | No dashboard or IPC authentication | Any reachable client can administer the service |
| P2 | Cache | Capacity is documented but never enforced | Unbounded growth |
| P2 | WAL | Always opens segment 0 and lexicographic ordering can be fragile | Restart/rotation correctness risk |
| P2 | Forecasting | eventslastsecond is actually "events from latest flush" | RPS forecasts use the wrong unit |
| P2 | ML/DNS | Several modules are heuristic stubs presented as advanced functionality | Misleading product behavior |

