apisetconfig() stores the patched configuration directly. Invalid shard counts, zero thresholds, or impossible timeouts can be introduced.

Validate before storing and return a useful error. The response type needs an error field or separate error response:

`rust
#[derive(Serialize)]
struct ConfigResponse {
    ok: bool,
    config: Option<Config>,
    error: Option<String>,
}
`

`rust
if let Err(error) = cfg.validate() {
    return (
        StatusCode::BADREQUEST,
        Json(ConfigResponse {
            ok: false,
            config: None,
            error: Some(error.tostring()),
        }),
    );
}

eng.config.store(Arc::new(cfg.clone()));
`

Patches replace entire sections

ConfigPatch uses complete EngineConfig, DetectionConfig, etc. A client changing one detection property must supply all required properties.

Create dedicated patch structs with optional fields:

`rust
#[derive(Debug, Deserialize)]
pub struct DetectionPatch {
    pub rpsthreshold: Option<u64>,
    pub blockttlsecs: Option<u64>,
    pub promoteminevents: Option<u32>,
